# Relaton SOTA roadmap

The goal state: **any standards reference, in any dialect, resolves to an
authoritative, versioned, provenance-carrying record — online or offline, in
any implementation — and renders faithfully in any house style.**

Seven layers. Each names its owner repo, the work, and the acceptance test.

## 1. Identifier semantics (pubid + flavors)

- [x] Formal identifier model: components, equivalence, and canonicalization
      written down as a spec (docs/identifier-model.adoc), one section per SDO
      family — identifier behavior is currently code with laws, not a
      specification with proofs.
      Delivered: docs/identifier-model.adoc (component model, Laws 0–4,
      equivalence-as-data requirement, a section per family).
- [x] Property-based tests as enforcement: parse(render(x)) == x,
      render(parse(x)) == render(x), exclude/parse idempotence, === antisymmetry
      — executed over every flavor's **full published corpus**, not fixtures.
      Delivered: spec/corpus/ (Laws 0, 1a, 1b, 2, 4 over every flavor with a
      published index), `rake spec:corpus`, and the nightly corpus workflow
      with deterministic slices and per-law known-failure manifests.
- [ ] Cross-SDO equivalence as DATA: joint publications, adoption chains
      (ISO → EN → BS EN), and variant spellings move from per-flavor logic into
      equivalence tables the resolver consults.
- [ ] The hard grammar edges each carry a pinned spec (OMG slashes and glued
      beta labels, ITS hyphens, NIST stage suffixes, the 30 non-trivial OMG
      acronyms).

## 2. Ingestion (data repos + flavor DataFetchers)

- [x] Source-capability matrix per SDO: what each source can
      enumerate / enrich / fetch, including stage coverage (CSRC carries
      drafts; the NIST-Tech-Pubs MODS does not — probed 2026-10-19).
      Delivered as docs/source-capability-matrix.adoc (static audit,
      2026-10-20).
- [ ] Incremental crawls: content-hash diffing replaces full rm -rf
      re-crawls.
- [x] Tombstones: withdrawn/delisted documents get markers instead of silent
      deletion.
      Delivered in the shared Crawler workflow (relaton/support#88):
      tombstones.yaml records id/file/timestamp/run for files git reports as
      deleted, and drops a marker when the same path is republished.
- [x] Per-record provenance: source, release tag, crawl timestamp on each
      record or sidecar.
      Delivered as the per-run sidecar provenance.json (repository, workflow,
      run id/attempt, source revision, crawler command, crawled_at) written by
      the shared Crawler workflow; flavor source URLs are in
      docs/source-capability-matrix.adoc, and tombstones carry their own
      timestamps.
- [x] Source-health dashboard + freshness SLAs — staleness is observed, not
      discovered (ITU-R sat dead for months before anyone measured it).
      Delivered: `bin/check-data-pages --freshness` (relaton/support#87) and
      the scheduled data-health workflow, which reports every data repo's
      machine-index age in the job summary and fails past a 48 h SLA.
- [x] ITU-R: headless-browser path (the CIE Ferrum machinery is the
      in-repo precedent) or the engagement outcome; the crawler's daily red
      ends.
      Decision: the server-rendered /pub + /rec crawl is the path; no headless
      browser is needed. The daily red was the data repo's stale rubyzip pin
      (relaton-data-itu-r#9). Verification run 39413400304 crawled, committed
      and pushed 5,427 files (commit 41d264f8) and refreshed index-v2.

## 3. Discovery (api + store)

- [ ] Cross-flavor query layer: filter/search by pubid components and relaton
      fields (the component-search requirement), pagination, facets.
- [ ] Stable record URIs; content negotiation: YAML / JSON / CSL-JSON /
      BibTeX / RIS / RDF.
- [x] The CF worker/API migration completes this layer.
      Delivered: api.relaton.org is served by Cloudflare Workers (`server:
      cloudflare`), the relaton-api-js ingest workflow is green, and the
      worker serves the collections / manifest / entries / search contract.

## 4. Graph integrity

- [x] Relation-coverage audit per SDO: what sources volunteer vs what exists.
      Delivered as docs/relation-coverage.adoc: 552,484 published records,
      42% with relations, 39% with status, bimodal per source; the adoption
      edges and the no-relation sources are called out.
- [ ] Adoption chains resolvable end-to-end (ISO → CEN → national) with
      bidirectional edges.
- [ ] Family/edition/all-parts views as first-class objects; edge round-trip
      laws (relations survive serialize/deserialize) tested like record
      round-trips.
      Edge round-trip laws delivered in relaton#324 (every relation type
      through YAML and XML, bidirectional pairs); the family/edition/all-parts
      views remain open.

## 5. Render fidelity

- [ ] Close the CitationStyle model-vs-code gaps (the known set).
- [x] CSL-JSON conformance as a tested contract.
      Delivered in relaton-ts: the renderer emits only CSL-JSON fields and
      types, routes editors/performers to their own fields, maps DOI/ISBN/ISSN,
      and `test/csl_conformance.test.ts` pins the invariants.
- [ ] Golden render corpora per SDO house style.

## 6. Data reproducibility

- [ ] Content-addressed dataset releases: versioned, hashed dataset artifacts
      per data repo.
- [x] Consumer-side pinning: a dataset lockfile so compilations reproduce
      years later.
      Delivered: `Relaton::Index::DatasetLock` captures the manifest's
      sha256/bytes and verifies a fetched artifact byte-for-byte; the lock is a
      lutaml-model YAML file.
- [ ] The machine index publishes per-release manifests alongside the rolling
      branch.

## 7. Conformance culture

- [ ] Shared Ruby/TypeScript conformance suite: the identifier and retrieval
      contracts both stacks execute (pubid parse/render/hash; index
      read/search).
- [ ] Grammar-level property fuzzing per flavor.
- [x] Fixture coverage metrics: per-SDO corpus coverage reported in CI.
      The corpus workflow reports each flavor's deserialized-row count
      against its full published index in the job summary.

## Open workstreams (already in flight)

- [ ] relaton#313/#314: the NIST CSRC supplement is merged — verify the data
      repo's next crawl brings stage-typed rows (NIST FIPS 197 ipd resolves to
      its own record); deliver the NIST engagement letter for historical
      drafts (write-up on relaton#313).
      Verified: relaton-data-nist v2 publishes 267 `ipd` rows, including
      data/nist-fips-197-ipd.yaml with docid `NIST FIPS 197 ipd`; live
      resolution was verified when relaton#318 merged. The engagement letter is
      an external communication the owner delivers.
- [x] relaton#75: the ITU-R source decision (see layer 2).
      The server-rendered /pub + /rec crawl is the path; the daily red was a
      dependency pin (relaton-data-itu-r#9/#10), not the source.
- [ ] isodoc#842 waits on pubid 2.0.0 final.
